6.2.6
Computing the Skew and Curvature analytically
For every model that one can deﬁne, we need to estimate the vector Ψ of model parameters from either the market
prices or their implied volatility quotes. When the parametric model is calibrated to the market quotes and the optimum
vector Ψ∗is obtained, the model call and put prices must equate the market ones. Since our model can retrieve
analytically European prices as well as Digital price, we show how to infer analytically the skew and curvature of the
IV surface for all strikes and maturities.
