It is an integer valued measure. A ﬁnite measure with mass 1 is called a probability measure.
Deﬁnition A.1.4 Let E ⊂Rd. A Radon measure on (E, B) is a measure µ such that for every compact measurable
set B ∈B, µ(B) < ∞.
A measure µ0 which gives zero mass to any point is said to be diffusive or atomless, that is ∀x ∈E, µ0({x}) = 0.
