A.2
Random variables
Deﬁnition A.2.1 A random variable is a function X : Ω→R with the property that {ω ∈Ω: X(ω) ≤x} ∈F for
each x ∈R.
Deﬁnition A.2.2 The distribution function of a random variable X is the function F : R →[0, 1] given by
F(x) = P(X ≤x)
A.2.1
Discrete random variables
